<title>POLAND: Poland offers 3-yr bonds to public at 101 zlotys.</title>
<headline>Poland offers 3-yr bonds to public at 101 zlotys.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish treasury said in a newspaper advertisement on Monday it will sell its three-year floating bond, due on November 6, 1999, to the public at an issue price of 101.00 zlotys.</p>
<p>It said the three-year bond, whose coupon is the average yield of four 13-week T-bill auctions before a interest period multiplied by 1.05, will be available to the public from November 4, 1996, to January 31, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
